  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Core Requirement**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the mandatory role of `firebase-integration-rpc` for Firebase Auth and Cloud Firestore. The critical first step is now clear: call `show_aistudio_ui` with `ui_type: \"firebase_setup\"` and immediately halt further execution. I can now proceed.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Setup Tasks**\n\nI am now grappling with the sequencing of setup tasks. Specifically, should I initiate `show_aistudio_ui` for Firebase first, or address the `set_up_oauth` for the Google Workspace integration? The prompt makes it clear that the Google ecosystem (Calendar, Drive, Gmail) is required, but both setup functions require stopping the execution to wait for user input, so I must choose one to initiate first. A review of `frontend-design` for dependencies is also required. I need to make a solid decision here!\n\n\n**Reviewing Design Documents**\n\nI am now deep diving into the reference files: `3_saas_dashboard.md`, `10_mobile_touch_apps.md`, `firestore-rules-and-blueprint.md`, and `error-handling-and-sdk.md`. I\'ve realized that the user needs to accept Firebase terms *before* any provisioning, so `show_aistudio_ui(ui_type: \"firebase_setup\")` must come first and halt execution. Afterward, on \"Turn 2\", I will implement `GetFirebaseTos` and `ProvisionFirebase`. We can then consider the Google Workspace OAuth flow. I\'m focusing on the dependency between these tasks.\n\n\n**Clarifying Sequential Actions**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that using interactive tools aligns with the desired implementation, specifically `show_aistudio_ui` for Firebase setup. My plan is to first read related Firebase and domain references, then call `show_aistudio_ui` with the \"firebase_setup\" UI type, and, as directed, immediately halt execution. This approach adheres to the constraints and establishes a clear sequential action plan.\n\n\n"
