    thinking: "**Verifying Dependency Compatibility**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that everything is now performing optimally. I\'m currently reviewing `package.json` to ensure the `@google/genai` dependency meets the minimum version requirement of 2.29.1, specifically targeting support for the gemini-3.8-* and gemini-4-hydrogen models. I have not completed this, but I am close.\n\n\n**Consolidating Package Installs**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the batched installation strategy. Remembering the `<environment_constraints>`, I\'m planning a single `install_applet_package` call. My goal is to install all dependencies \342\200\223 `firebase`, `recharts`, `@google/genai@latest`, `eslint`, and `@firebase/eslint-plugin-security-rules` \342\200\223 in one go, as specified.\n\n\n**Formulating Comprehensive Architecture**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the architecture for LIFE OS, as per Section 1 of ultra-mode. We have the app name, LIFE OS, with a tagline in Arabic, and are considering our default language and direction. I\'m focusing on RTL for Arabic and LTR for English, and thinking in detail about Egyptian-friendly wording. Currency is set to Egyptian Pound, and I\'m ensuring all monetary values are stored as integer minor units to prevent floating-point errors.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Language**\n\nI\'m now establishing the LIFE OS visual system, starting with a meticulous 60-30-10 palette. I\'m choosing deep charcoal as the foundation, crisp white for primary typography, and a soft emerald/sage for actions. I\'m avoiding any unnecessary complexity, like nested card sandwiches and pulsing status dots. Clear rules govern the use of amber and crimson for warnings, and I\'m avoiding the default fonts. I am designing every font from scratch.\n\n\n**Specifying Typeface Parameters**\n\nI\'m now setting typography. I\'ve selected `Roboto` (primary display/body) and `JetBrains Mono` for tabular numerals in financial figures, timers, and metrics, ensuring strict `tabular-nums` formatting for all monetary values, percentages, steps, timers, and dates. I\'m focusing on responsiveness, designing a compact mobile experience and a full desktop presence. The layout adapts for mobile (compact sticky top and bottom bars, bottom sheet modals) and desktop (right-anchored sidebar, three-zone top bar, responsive dashboard). I am also implementing a clear disclosure of integrated live services, as per policy.\n\n\n**Evaluating Platform APIs**\n\nI am now comparing `server.ts`\'s Web Speech API implementation, incorporating Egyptian Arabic Gemini parsing and CSV/JSON/PDF export features, against the capabilities of native Android APIs. I\'m focusing on the trade-offs between manual logging on the web and the integrated functionalities of Android Health Connect, Xiaomi Smart Band sync, Android Usage Stats API, and Google Calendar/Drive/Gmail OAuth. I\'m also ensuring clear indicators are displayed for service availability.\n\n\n**Designing User Account Management**\n\nI\'m now implementing account management to improve usability. I\'m focusing on a streamlined process to accommodate instant usability and Firebase Auth. A subtle \"Sign in with Google to sync cloud\" option is being considered for the sidebar/account panel, alongside an Onboarding/Profile editor. Onboarding is accessible from Settings and via a banner, with `?autostart=1` support.\n\n\n\n**Developing Daily Briefing**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the AI daily briefing feature. I\'m focusing on a real server-side Gemini API call using `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` to generate concise Arabic/English financial, productivity, and health insights. The insights will include 1\342\200\2232 actionable recommendations derived from actual, structured user metrics. I\'m also ensuring error handling and clear presentation of unavailable metrics. I\'m thinking about including a quick action bar with options for voice/text expense entry, quick task add, and a quick energy check-in. I\'m also focused on building in functionality for manual expense input.\n\n\n**Implementing Expense Input**\n\nI\'m now building the expense input system. I\'m focusing on features such as creating custom categories, entering dates, selecting payment methods, adding notes, and toggling recurring expenses. I am also implementing a voice-based Egyptian Arabic parser using the Web Speech API (`ar-EG`), along with a text input field, and example. I will then call `/api/ai/parse-expense` to ensure validation. A mandatory Confirmation Card will always be displayed, and there will be a search, category filter, and delete function.\n\n\n**Constructing Financial Tools**\n\nI\'m now building the budgeting, savings goals, and investment tracking features. For budgets, I\'m implementing monthly and category budgets with live spending percentages, amber and crimson alerts, and actual vs. planned comparisons. Savings goals will include calculations for remaining amounts, progress percentages, target dates, and suggested monthly contributions. The investment tracker will handle gold, stocks, mutual funds, and ETFs with detailed quantity, prices, fees, and profit/loss tracking, clearly labeling manual valuations.\n\n\n\n**Constructing Task Management**\n\nI\'m now building the calendar and focus mode features. I\'m focusing on weekly and daily schedule views, with the ability to create, edit, and delete events, which always require confirmation. I am implementing personal and work calendar filters, along with a Google Calendar sync status card to indicate the connection state. For focus mode, I\'m integrating live countdown timers, pause, resume and reset functionality, and a session history log with daily focus statistics. I am also implementing a distraction counter.\n\n\n**Analyzing Energy Intelligence**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the Energy Intelligence module. I am focusing on integrating several elements: sleep and activity analytics that includes charts for weekly sleep duration and consistency, steps vs daily target progress, and a non-medical observations disclaimer. I am building a transparent, weighted estimation model based on sleep, consistency, activity, screen time and a self-report that will incorporate a 30-day baseline tracker, a daily self-check-in form, and measured vs. inferred insight separation. Finally, there\'s the Digital Wellbeing aspect. This includes app category usage, nighttime phone usage, focus interruptions, a weekly screen time chart, and a manual log entry.\n\n\n**Refining AI Interaction**\n\nI\'m now integrating an AI interaction strategy. I am using `gemini-4-hydrogen` for deep analysis. I\'m focusing on \"Minimal Context Injection\" so that I\'m sending only relevant metrics, with a non-medical disclaimer. Also important is AI action proposals, and confirmation cards. I\'m creating an \"AI Usage & Cost Quota Panel\". Lastly, I\'m thinking about Personal Goals and Reports and Insights sections.\n\n\n**Defining Data Export Strategies**\n\nI\'m now implementing PDF export, alongside JSON backup and CSV financial data exports. I am including clear privacy disclosures and connection statuses for linked accounts like Google Auth, Calendar, Drive, and Gmail, with read-only financial email parsing and manual input validation. The `settings` section is being built, which includes an editable user profile for all default settings. The account defaults are clearly defined.\n\n\n\n**Establishing Server Configuration**\n\nI\'ve completed the server.ts implementation with the specified routes: `/api/ai/briefing`, `/api/ai/parse-expense`, `/api/ai/chat`, and `/api/ai/goal-milestones`. I\'m now integrating the `@google/genai` client, including API key handling and a user-agent header. The server is using a rate limiting strategy. I\'m focusing on ensuring robust error handling throughout the API.\n\n\n**Securing Firebase Data**\n\nI\'m now implementing robust Firebase security rules. I\'m focusing on ensuring zero cross-user leakage. I am using `/users/{userId}/...` for all user collections and enforcing strict PII isolation. I am now working on the Eight Pillars workflow: creating the `firebase-blueprint.json`, `security_spec.md`, `DRAFT_firestore.rules`, and `eslint.config.mjs` with `@firebase/eslint-plugin-security-rules`. I\'m using `isOwner(userId)`, `isVerifiedUser()`, strict `isValid[Entity]` schema validation, `isValidId()`, `.size()` checks, `affectedKeys().hasOnly()`, and immutable fields with `createdAt == request.time`.\n\n\n**Finalizing Security Protocols**\n\nI\'m now in the final stages, having successfully linted the code to eliminate all errors and finalized the `firestore.rules`. My next step is to deploy the rules via `rpc_action` with `fax.DeployRules`. The Firebase security rules are now in place. I have completed the eight pillar workflow, and completed data validation and zero cross-user leakage. I am now working on pure logic modules and unit tests.\n\nI\'m now implementing the unit tests and associated logic for the financial utilities. I\'ve completed implementing functions for EGP conversion and available cash balance calculation (excluding unpaid freelance income). The tests also cover net worth, budget utilization, savings goals, and investment P/L calculations. I am also working on transparent non-medical energy score calculations.\n\n\n**Testing Financial Invariants**\n\nI\'m now implementing unit tests for energy and scheduling. I am focusing on verifying that all financial calculations meet their invariants. These calculations include piasters math, excluding unpaid freelance income, and calculations for net worth, budget utilization, and investment profit/loss. The tests also account for baseline day counts and graceful re-weighting when metrics are missing. Smart scheduling helpers also prioritize deep work slots.\n\n\n**Executing Package Installs**\n\nI\'m now proceeding with the batched package installation and the metadata and index.html updates. I\'ve begun integrating the single `install_applet_package` call, targeting `metadata.json` and `index.html` for synchronization of the title, description, and font specifications. The goal is to ensure a unified configuration and streamline setup.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "CboDa7fBBZCcz7IPneiWwQg"
