    thinking: "**Verifying Installation Success**\n\nOkay, great news! I\'ve confirmed a clean installation of all packages. Now, I\'m shifting focus to `package.json`. My plan is to modify the `\"dev\"` and `\"start\"` scripts using `tsx server.ts`. I also need to make sure to create the global CSS file (`src/index.css`), along with `firebase-blueprint.json`, `security_spec.md`, and `eslint.config.mjs`.\n\n\n**Checking Package.json Scripts**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of the `package.json` scripts, making sure I align with the guidelines. I\'ve re-examined the scripts to ensure they adhere to `<environment_constraints>` and `<framework>`. Based on this analysis, I\'ll update `\"dev\": \"tsx server.ts\"` to ensure compatibility.\n\n\n**Refining Package Script Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on ensuring `server.ts` is pure TypeScript without advanced features like enums or parameter properties, for Node 22 compatibility. The next step is a deep dive into the blueprint file and Firestore rules, designing both to pass security checks and satisfy all pillars of hardened rules. I\'m also carefully defining Firestore collections, prioritizing user privacy and zero PII exposure, strictly scoping data to `/users/{userId}`. I\'m ensuring all data, such as income, expenses, and budgets, belong to the individual user.\n\n\n**Mapping User Data Structure**\n\nI\'m now detailing user-specific Firestore collections. I\'ve mapped several areas, including savings goals, manual investments, tasks, calendar events, focus session logs, health metrics, app usage, energy check-ins, and personal goals. The structure prioritizes strict privacy with scoped data like `/users/{userId}/...` and careful PII avoidance. Each collection will be meticulously defined.\n\n\n**Defining AI Usage Tracking**\n\nI\'m now detailing AI usage tracking. I\'m focusing on `/users/{userId}/ai_usage/{usageId}`, ensuring strict security. This includes `isVerifiedOwner(userId)` checks, global deny rules, `isValidId()` for path variable validation (not list operations), and rigorous data validation with helpers like `isValid[Entity](incoming(), userId)`.  I\'m also paying close attention to identity integrity (`data.userId == userId`), field restrictions (keys, sizes, array bounds, temporal integrity, action-based key control).\n\n\n"
