  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Crafting UI Components**\n\nI\'m now focused on building modular and clean UI components. I\'m taking into account various design disciplines from frontend design principles and referencing materials like `3_saas_dashboard.md` and `10_mobile_touch_apps.md`. My next step is to carefully check our UI craft standards before moving forward.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Style**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the visual style for the UI. I\'m focusing on very quiet metadata display with `/` separators, and proper `<button>` elements, instead of any decorative pulsing dots or thick accent borders. I\'m committed to single-elevation depth with a flat dark charcoal surface, hairline borders, and generous whitespace. I\'m also ensuring a soft green accent for the primary CTA buttons, active navigation states, and progress bars.\n\n\n**Implementing Tabular Numerals**\n\nI\'m now implementing `font-mono-nums` for all numerical data like amounts, percentages, and steps. I\'m also ensuring full accessibility with native controls, appropriate ARIA labels, and touch target sizes. I\'ve calculated the mobile sticky cap to be under 15% to allow more viewing real estate. I\'m also creating a top bar contract that includes a brand title, navigation, and a primary action. I\'m organizing the UI with `ConfirmDialog` and `VoiceExpenseModal` components for clean code and reusability.\n\n\n**Designing Modular Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the architecture for Arabic expense entry, supporting voice input in `ar-EG` and providing example phrases. I\'m building out three modules: a Unified Home Dashboard in `HomeDashboard.tsx` for quick summaries; a Finance Module in `FinanceModule.tsx` with expense and income analysis and voice entry; and a Time Module in `TimeModule.tsx` for task management and scheduling.\n\n\n**Developing New Modules**\n\nI\'m now adding new modules, specifically for Health & Energy (`HealthEnergyModule.tsx`) incorporating fitness data and manual logging, and Digital Wellbeing (`WellbeingModule.tsx`) with screen time analysis. I\'m also planning a LIFE AI chat assistant (`LifeAiModule.tsx`) with domain selection and AI usage tracking. Finally, I\'m working on a Goals module (`GoalsModule.tsx`) to track personal progress across categories.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "LcIDa_zEKYSsqtsPl-fA6AI"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_6024804069680063088"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import React from \'react\';\\nimport { X } from \'lucide-react\';\\n\\ninterface ConfirmDialogProps {\\n  open: boolean;\\n  title: string;\\n  description: string;\\n  confirmLabel: string;\\n  cancelLabel: string;\\n  tone?: \'primary\' | \'danger\';\\n  onConfirm: () => void;\\n  onCancel: () => void;\\n}\\n\\nexport const ConfirmDialog: React.FC<ConfirmDialogProps> = ({\\n  open,\\n  title,\\n  description,\\n  confirmLabel,\\n  cancelLabel,\\n  tone = \'primary\',\\n  onConfirm,\\n  onCancel,\\n}) => {\\n  if (!open) return null;\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div\\n      className=\\\"fixed inset-0 z-50 flex items-end sm:items-center justify-center bg-black/70 backdrop-blur-sm p-4\\\"\\n      role=\\\"dialog\\\"\\n      aria-modal=\\\"true\\\"\\n      aria-labelledby=\\\"confirm-dialog-title\\\"\\n    >\\n      <div className=\\\"w-full max-w-md bg-[#13171C] border border-[#232A33] rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-5\\\">\\n        <div className=\\\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\\\">\\n          <h2 id=\\\"confirm-dialog-title\\\" className=\\\"text-base font-semibold text-[#F4F6F8]\\\">\\n            {title}\\n          </h2>\\n          <button\\n            type=\\\"button\\\"\\n            onClick={onCancel}\\n            aria-label={cancelLabel}\\n            className=\\\"min-h-[36px] min-w-[36px] flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-[#8E99A8] hover:text-[#F4F6F8] hover:bg-[#1C222B] transition-colors\\\"\\n          >\\n            <X className=\\\"w-4 h-4\\\" />\\n          </button>\\n        </div>\\n\\n        <p className=\\\"text-sm text-[#A9B3C1] leading-relaxed\\\">{description}</p>\\n\\n        <div className=\\\"flex items-center justify-end gap-3 pt-1\\\">\\n          <button\\n            type=\\\"button\\\"\\n            onClick={onCancel}\\n            className=\\\"min-h-[44px] px-4 py-2 rounded-xl border border-[#232A33] text-sm font-medium text-[#C8D0DC] hover:bg-[#1B212A] transition-colors whitespace-nowrap\\\"\\n          >\\n            {cancelLabel}\\n          </button>\\n          <button\\n            type=\\\"button\\\"\\n            onClick={onConfirm}\\n            className={`min-h-[44px] px-5 py-2 rounded-xl text-sm font-semibold transition-colors whitespace-nowrap ${\\n              tone === \'danger\'\\n                ? \'bg-red-500 text-white hover:bg-red-400\'\\n                : \'bg-emerald-500 text-[#07110C] hover:bg-emerald-400\'\\n            }`}\\n          >\\n            {confirmLabel}\\n          </button>\\n        </div>\\n      </div>\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n};\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create accessible ConfirmDialog component replacing native alerts/confirms for sensitive actions\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/ConfirmDialog.tsx\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating ConfirmDialog component\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create ConfirmDialog\"}"
