  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Visual Patterns**\n\nI\'m struck by the wealth of information gleaned from the provided screenshots, particularly `r1-finance.png`, `r1-desktop.png`, `r1-mobile.png`, and `r1-en-ltr.png`. Every click, state transition, and timer (like `24:59`), as well as the RTL-to-LTR flip, has provided a massive amount of insights.\n\n\n**Analyzing Visual Impact**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the impact of visual bugs, especially those exposed during initial render. That Recharts PieChart issue? It\'s a critical, high-impact problem. The animation, taking ~1500ms, causes the pie chart to look collapsed and incomplete on render. I\'ve also found an issue related to the Arabic text rendering within the `font-mono-nums`. I\342\200\231m looking at concrete fixes, like disabling those animations and focusing on instantaneous, full-fidelity chart display.\n\n\n**Refining Font Rendering**\n\nI\'m now zeroed in on Arabic font rendering. The \"JetBrains Mono\" font, while good for English, awkwardly spaces out Arabic letters, as seen in `r1-desktop.png` and `r1-mobile.png`. The `\330\254 . \331\205`, `\330\243 \330\263 \330\247 \330\263`, and `\331\210 \330\266 \330\271` are particularly problematic, even within the context of numerical data. My fix involves modifying the CSS to prioritize \"Cairo\" for Arabic fallback, ensuring consistent and correct glyph display, and keeping `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;`. I\'ve also noted a line-wrapping issue with longer Arabic numbers.\n\n\n**Adjusting Line Breaks**\n\nI\'m now focused on line breaks with Arabic and currency, specifically preventing breaks in figures like `28,000 \330\254.\331\205` by using `tabular-nums` and `whitespace-nowrap`. I\'m removing the use of `font-mono-nums` from elements that contain full Arabic prose, such as the example dates, and applying the `tabular-nums` property to Arabic sentences more generally. I\'ve found an error in the \"Time Intelligence Focus Mode\" (in `r1-en-ltr.png`) where the `focusLabel` didn\'t update to English after a language switch, which I am fixing with a `useEffect` hook in `TimeModule.tsx` that triggers on `lang` changes. Finally, I\'m noting the bottom \"AI Daily Briefing\" card on desktop needs a slight adjustment.\n\n\n"
