  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Crafting Feature Integrity**\n\nI\'m focused on seamlessly integrating this feature into LIFE OS, ensuring complete adherence to Firebase security rules and blueprint synchronization. I\'m also meticulously reviewing the Frontend Design Constitution\'s guidelines, particularly concerning zero-pill metadata, dark-mode optimization, and minimal data-driven surfaces. This will guarantee a robust and elegant solution.\n\n\n**Defining Data Model**\n\nI\'ve outlined the core data model for the \"Daily Micro-Goal\" feature. I\'ve begun defining the `DailyMicroGoal` interface within `/src/types/lifeos.ts`. It includes `id`, `userId`, `date`, `title`, `category`, `targetValue`, `currentValue`, `unit`, and `completed` properties, with specified types and constraints. Next, I\'ll integrate this into the Firebase data flow.\n\n\n**Determining Data Location**\n\nI\'ve determined the optimal placement for Daily Micro-Goals, opting for a dedicated subcollection: `/users/{userId}/daily_micro_goals/{goalId}`. This aligns perfectly with the existing structure and principles found in `LifeOsContext.tsx`, `firebase-blueprint.json`, and `firestore.rules`. I plan to integrate `dailyMicroGoals: DailyMicroGoal[]` within `LifeOsDataset`. I\'m now contemplating seeding the data, balancing a pre-populated goal versus an initial empty state to enhance the user experience and immediate progress visibility within the `HomeDashboard`.\n\n\n**Implementing Starter Goals**\n\nI\'ve crafted a sensible starter micro-goal that immediately showcases the progress card on first load. The micro-goal is designed to be immediately useful with a sensible starter value, allowing a quick demonstration of the feature. Furthermore, I\'ve checked `LifeOsContext.tsx` and am adding the needed functions: `upsertDailyMicroGoal`, `updateDailyMicroGoalProgress`, and `deleteDailyMicroGoal`. Finally, I\'m binding the `daily_micro_goals` collection to `dailyMicroGoals`.\n\n\n**Refining Data Integrity**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating `dailyMicroGoals` into the `seedCloudFromSample` batch seed, ensuring it\'s included within the snapshot, and that the data is preserved during `loadLocalDataset()`. Next, I\'ll update `/firebase-blueprint.json` to define the `DailyMicroGoal` entity and path, and I\'ll update `/security_spec.md` with the necessary invariant. Lastly, I will update `/firestore.rules` meticulously, following the rigorous workflow to ensure security. I need to make certain `isValidDailyMicroGoal(data, userId)` validates all the required data keys.\n\n\n**Validating Security Rules**\n\nI am now meticulously refining the Firebase security rules. I am focused on the `isValidDailyMicroGoal()` function to validate data integrity. Specifically, I\'m checking for required keys, `userId`, `date`, `title`, and so on, confirming all keys are present, and the size limits are met. I am also checking against allowed categories, as well as the data types. I\'m focusing on the `match` block under `/users/{userId}` to finalize the security layer.\n\n\n**Finalizing Security Layer**\n\nI am now meticulously scrutinizing the Firebase security rules for `daily_micro_goals`. I\'ve incorporated robust update rules, ensuring data integrity and preventing unauthorized modifications. I\'m focusing on validating updates: ensuring the `userId` remains unchanged and allowing only specified keys to be altered, like `date`, `title`, `category`, and others. I\'m also double-checking `isValidId`, `affectedKeys().hasOnly`, and the time stamps. I\'m taking extreme care, focusing on the `match` block under `/users/{userId}` to finalize the security layer. I also must make sure `upsertDailyMicroGoal` sanitizes and truncates data on the client side.\n\n\n**Designing Modal Implementation**\n\nI\'m now focused on the new modal component. I\'m building `/src/components/DailyMicroGoalModal.tsx`, which mirrors `VoiceExpenseModal.tsx` in design, per the Frontend Design Constitution. I\'m ensuring accessibility features like `role`, `aria-*` attributes, and escape-to-close functionality are implemented. I\'m creating a dark, mobile-friendly design with a `max-w-lg` constraint. I\'m prioritizing user experience with quick-entry template buttons and validating all inputs. I am working on the quick templates, title, target value, current value, and unit fields.\n\n\n**Constructing Modal Fields**\n\nI\'m now implementing the modal form fields. I\'ve designed fields for: Title, Category (with interactive buttons: Focus, Finance, Health, Wellbeing, Personal), Target Value and Unit (with number inputs), and Current Progress (also number input). I\'m focusing on accessible design with zero pills, touch targets, and ensuring a great user experience with input validation and quick entry.\n\n\n**Visualizing Quick Action**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Daily Micro-Goal feature into the HomeDashboard. I\'m adding a button, titled \"Daily Micro-Goal,\" to the Greeting & Quick Actions Row, positioned alongside the \"Voice Expense\" and \"Ask LIFE AI\" buttons. Below the Greeting Row, I\'m rendering the Daily Micro-Goal Progress Card. This card will display metadata, a title with status, progress as a fraction, a percentage, and a progress bar. I\'m prioritizing interactive quick controls directly on the card.\n\n\n**Implementing Progress Card**\n\nI\'m now implementing the Daily Micro-Goal Progress Card in `HomeDashboard.tsx`. I\'m designing interactive controls within the progress card, including decrement and increment buttons with smart stepping, and a \"Mark Done\" toggle. An \"Edit\" button will open the `DailyMicroGoalModal`. In the empty state, I\'ll display a card explaining the feature and a button to set a goal, which will trigger the modal.\n\n\n"
