  planner_response {
    response: "Added the **Daily Micro-Goal** modal and top-of-dashboard progress card to **LIFE OS**:\n\n### What Was Added\n- **Daily Micro-Goal Modal**:\n  - Accessible dialog triggered directly from the Home Dashboard action bar (`\331\207\330\257\331\201 \330\247\331\204\331\212\331\210\331\205 \330\247\331\204\331\205\330\265\330\272\331\221\330\261` / `Daily Micro-Goal`) as well as from the progress card\'s edit or empty-state button.\n  - Supports Arabic (RTL) and English (LTR) with quick presets, area selection (`Focus`, `Finance`, `Health`, `Wellbeing`, `Personal`), custom title, target value, current progress, measurement unit, and a **Clear Goal** action when editing an existing goal.\n- **Top Dashboard Progress Card**:\n  - Pinned at the top of the Home Dashboard above the financial and energy cards.\n  - Displays the active micro-goal title, category, explicit completion status, tabular numeric progress (`current / target unit` and `%`), and an RTL/LTR-aware progress bar.\n  - Includes inline controls to increment/decrement progress in smart steps, toggle completion, or open the modal to edit/clear. Shows a clean empty state prompt when cleared.\n- **Persistence & Firestore Sync**:\n  - Persists locally in browser storage immediately and syncs to Firestore under `/users/{userId}/daily_micro_goals/{goalId}` when signed in with Google.\n  - Updated the data schema blueprint and security rules (`isValidDailyMicroGoal`), validated with ESLint (0 errors), and deployed the rules to Firestore.\n\n### Verification\n- `compile_applet`, `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit`), `eslint firestore.rules`, and all 9 unit tests passed cleanly, and the development server has been restarted.\n\n*Note on Firestore Security Rules*: While the added owner-scoped validation rules for `daily_micro_goals` were linted and deployed, please review and further harden your `firestore.rules` before sharing the application broadly."
    message_id: "2_EDa4mOFdK9vdIPloKX6A4"
    modified_response: "Added the **Daily Micro-Goal** modal and top-of-dashboard progress card to **LIFE OS**:\n\n### What Was Added\n- **Daily Micro-Goal Modal**:\n  - Accessible dialog triggered directly from the Home Dashboard action bar (`\331\207\330\257\331\201 \330\247\331\204\331\212\331\210\331\205 \330\247\331\204\331\205\330\265\330\272\331\221\330\261` / `Daily Micro-Goal`) as well as from the progress card\'s edit or empty-state button.\n  - Supports Arabic (RTL) and English (LTR) with quick presets, area selection (`Focus`, `Finance`, `Health`, `Wellbeing`, `Personal`), custom title, target value, current progress, measurement unit, and a **Clear Goal** action when editing an existing goal.\n- **Top Dashboard Progress Card**:\n  - Pinned at the top of the Home Dashboard above the financial and energy cards.\n  - Displays the active micro-goal title, category, explicit completion status, tabular numeric progress (`current / target unit` and `%`), and an RTL/LTR-aware progress bar.\n  - Includes inline controls to increment/decrement progress in smart steps, toggle completion, or open the modal to edit/clear. Shows a clean empty state prompt when cleared.\n- **Persistence & Firestore Sync**:\n  - Persists locally in browser storage immediately and syncs to Firestore under `/users/{userId}/daily_micro_goals/{goalId}` when signed in with Google.\n  - Updated the data schema blueprint and security rules (`isValidDailyMicroGoal`), validated with ESLint (0 errors), and deployed the rules to Firestore.\n\n### Verification\n- `compile_applet`, `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit`), `eslint firestore.rules`, and all 9 unit tests passed cleanly, and the development server has been restarted.\n\n*Note on Firestore Security Rules*: While the added owner-scoped validation rules for `daily_micro_goals` were linted and deployed, please review and further harden your `firestore.rules` before sharing the application broadly."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    thinking_signature: "\022\357\003\n\354\003\001i\024}\023g\221\\\301[H\315\006}\bp\337X\357\020Z\3070\331C\340E\032\251\264\034\274\033\345\rRG-p\267}\245\225k\315\374\224\332G\353k?\006\266\236r`\236\266\232\350\244\325$\t!o\336\006nOpq\320\260\034\332\251\201Le)\v&\305\037=\262Q\336\317)\254\247\365V\004\224\322\311\314)\362\374\330\370\317!\tL\273l\241m-F\256}\276X\201\245s\200\257\356u\234>b\030Z\344\000\213\352\265)\254S\231g\323q\275\2703[\031\030\030\336r\310{/\034&<h\326\a\345\371\023\372R\303Y\356\t\247\326\343\206\032\306\320\221\254\v\221\255\226<kz\231#-@\301\'\n\360#\225?E\223\000\273\210\217\326!I\310\026\024N\266\"D\001\377\236\3310H\227\316\230\350i\224\033j$&m$\200\351unY\2616\301\204\313\031`\255\341v\003\251\344\344\035\321D\362\251\270\357\364;\355\347(\f\351\032\320\272+\317\034\256\307\247\216\337\035}\267*\377\272\320?\363\024O:q\001Sua\226\345\237\314\331\2240\031\241\265O\"\365F\205\353\300\377\251\v\226~q.\367\304\271 Z\214\017\337\255p\036\247\352T\340\360\210\375\342\021\255\244\'\245\004\001\305\212|%\256\212\334\v\343\022/\217\222\315\222u\211w\307\320M\336S\353\357g|#I\322L\336,\325\251\270Q\031g\212\034o\t\370\350\b\022\a\0250\357\375\016\273\365\265q\215\b\351\021\bO@\261\2175+\232\211@\224\200\223\232\203M\0033\\\215?\242i}\304g\031\177\026,\276Wo\242d\265\241\316\346\305\320X\221\311\265\346\004\360\260\276\344T4\n\3218\306d6\201GkhK\366,*\b\200y\257k\354U\032\026\243\221\005\354\f\223\276\266\247=\257\273"
