    thinking: "**Considering AI\'s Autonomy**\n\nI\'m wrestling with the user\'s question about AI modifying the program itself. Can the AI within the system alter its own code to add or remove features? The core inquiry centers on self-modification and autonomy. I\'m exploring the implications of enabling such self-directed changes within the architecture.\n\n\n**Clarifying Code Modification**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the critical distinction between runtime and development-time modification. The core question is about the AI altering its own underlying code at runtime. It\'s a \"no\" for the runtime AI in the app; however, the request to add or remove code happens here in the development environment. It\'s crucial to address the user\'s question with accuracy.\n\n\n**Exploring Dynamic Customization**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user-permitted dynamic adjustments. I can enable the system to efficiently and securely modify application data and configurations. This includes adding/removing daily expenses, income, budgets, tasks, appointments, goals, and custom categories. Also, I\'m now exploring dynamic UI control, such as showing/hiding widgets, re-arranging sections, and modifying settings. All with user confirmation of course!\n\n\n"
